(6948623, 1046421, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixelpig:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1038123" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg"/></a> <br/>The Flying Pig awarded in recognition of fine art created with photography, especially in Expert editing challenges. See previous awards &amp; comments in <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1171726&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Flying Pig</a> thread.<br/> <br/>The title is like a line from a poem or song. The drama of light &amp; shadow, the sense of a story, allows my imagination to create its own narrative. That''s better treat than the finest champagne. After I enjoy the semi-familiar in this work of art, my gaze settles on the unfamiliar. The white light dripping on the wall, the animalistic shadow with one white paw draped over the corner, the doll''s face with the reflective nose. Or is it a window? I''m left wondering if these friends live only in your wallet. It feels a little sad.<br/> <br/>Cheers to you for this excellent work of art. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well deserved.</td>', 'Originally posted by pixelpig:  The Flying Pig awarded in recognition of fine art created with photography, especially in Expert editing challenges. See previous awards & comments in The Flying Pig thread. The title is like a line from a poem or song. The drama of light & shadow, the sense of a story, allows my imagination to create its own narrative. That''s better treat than the finest champagne. After I enjoy the semi-familiar in this work of art, my gaze settles on the unfamiliar. The white light dripping on the wall, the animalistic shadow with one white paw draped over the corner, the doll''s face with the reflective nose. Or is it a window? I''m left wondering if these friends live only in your wallet. It feels a little sad. Cheers to you for this excellent work of art.   Well deserved.', '2013-01-04 00:09:55.000000', NULL, 0),
