(6949338, 1046713, 108069, '<td valign="top">I can''t really imagine this not being a FS blue, so it''s a bit shocking to see it second to anything, but Gyaban''s was wonderfully bizarre and interesting. Incredible photo.<br/> <br/>Edit: Ha! Joke''s on me. I thought this was real. Well, that just shows your excellent PS skills. Well done.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-01-04 22:07:02.</i></td>', 'I can''t really imagine this not being a FS blue, so it''s a bit shocking to see it second to anything, but Gyaban''s was wonderfully bizarre and interesting. Incredible photo. Edit: Ha! Joke''s on me. I thought this was real. Well, that just shows your excellent PS skills. Well done.', '2013-01-04 22:04:53.000000', '2013-01-04 22:07:02.000000', 0),
(6949348, 1046640, 40391, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GAP2012:</b></div><hr/><i> its unfortunate that you decided to enter this and hope you dont feel dispondant at the result, it was higher than i would have expected it to go... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your concern Gary but I was not disappointed at all and it was just about where I had expected it to finish. I''m not too sure why you would consider it unfortunate unless you felt it was unfortunate that you had to view it. If that was the case I''m sorry if the image offended you. <br/> <br/>I was very surprised at how much it looked like the dog was abut to eat the cat when I reviewed the image as they get along quite well and were just playing. What I liked abut the image and why I entered it was that for me it captured an interesting bit of action and the colours nicely added to the shot.  I usually convert to B&amp;W unless the colours really appeal to me.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-01-04 22:36:31.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by GAP2012: its unfortunate that you decided to enter this and hope you dont feel dispondant at the result, it was higher than i would have expected it to go...   Thanks for your concern Gary but I was not disappointed at all and it was just about where I had expected it to finish. I''m not too sure why you would consider it unfortunate unless you felt it was unfortunate that you had to view it. If that was the case I''m sorry if the image offended you.  I was very surprised at how much it looked like the dog was abut to eat the cat when I reviewed the image as they get along quite well and were just playing. What I liked abut the image and why I entered it was that for me it captured an interesting bit of action and the colours nicely added to the shot.  I usually convert to B&W unless the colours really appeal to me.', '2013-01-04 22:29:29.000000', '2013-01-04 22:36:31.000000', 0),
